+    // declared inside that block, so the read was of a dead stack slot -- the
+    // same shape BlendRot avoids by declaring its qtemp out here. MWCC kept the
+    // slot alive and the original worked by accident; GCC reuses it, and the
+    // mirrored path then blended whatever landed there. On the root node that
+    // is the whole character's height, which is the players-float bug.
+    nlVector3 vtemp;
     if (bMirror)
     {
